    <tags>cota claude usage limits quota tray windows monitoring</tags>
    <summary>Your Claude usage limits, in the Windows tray</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
A ring in the notification area that fills as your Claude usage limits do, so
you find out you are near the wall before you hit it rather than mid-task.

Left-click for a panel with every bucket - session, weekly, per-model - the
time until each resets, and an estimate of when the fullest one will fill at
your current rate. Toasts at 50%, 80% and 95%.

A single 1 MB executable with no runtime dependencies, sitting in the tray
using about 5 MB and effectively no CPU.

* Reads the token Claude Code already stores; never asks for a credential.
* Talks to api.anthropic.com and nowhere else.
* Projects when you will hit the cap from the slope of your own usage.
* Attributes the week to projects, read from local transcripts.

Requires Claude Code, signed in at least once on this machine.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/kidchenko/cota/releases</releaseNotes>
